%% Diagram: Data Quality Incident Response Flow
%% Purpose : Maps the decision path from a data quality alert through
%%           quarantine, root-cause investigation, stakeholder notification,
%%           and pipeline restoration.
%% Usage   : Render with Mermaid CLI or the GitHub Mermaid renderer.
%%           Referenced by runbooks/data_quality_incident.md
flowchart TD
    A(["🔔 Data Quality Alert Fires\n(Great Expectations / PSI threshold breached)"]) --> B

    B{"Schema valid?\nNo unexpected nulls,\ntype changes, or drops?"}

    B -- No --> C["Quarantine affected batch\nWrite to dead-letter table\nTag records with incident ID"]
    B -- Yes --> D["Inspect statistical thresholds\nCompare distribution vs baseline\nCheck PSI score"]

    C --> E["Identify upstream source\nLog affected date range\nCapture raw sample"]
    D --> F{"PSI > 0.20?\n(high distribution shift)"}

    F -- Yes --> G["Classify as SEV-2 incident\nPage data engineering on-call\nOpen incident in tracker"]
    F -- No --> H["Classify as SEV-3 investigation\nAssign to next-day triage\nAdd monitoring annotation"]

    E --> G

    G --> I["Notify dependent ML models\nSuppress live scoring if necessary\nSend stakeholder update T+15m"]
    H --> J["Increase alert sensitivity\nSchedule follow-up review"]

    I --> K{"Root cause confirmed?"}
    K -- No --> L["Escalate to SEV-1\nLoops back to E for deeper dig"]
    K -- Yes --> M["Apply fix or reject bad batch\nRerun affected pipeline"]

    L --> E
    M --> N["Validate output against SLA\nCompare row counts and metrics"]

    N --> O{"Validation passed?"}
    O -- No --> M
    O -- Yes --> P["Unquarantine clean records\nResume downstream consumers"]

    P --> Q["Write postmortem\nUpdate alert thresholds\nClose incident"]

    style A fill:#f59e0b,color:#000
    style G fill:#ef4444,color:#fff
    style H fill:#f97316,color:#fff
    style Q fill:#22c55e,color:#fff
    style L fill:#dc2626,color:#fff
